    <string name="settings_help">Notes:\n· Area ratio = box area in this analysed frame ÷ box area in the previous one, where area = width × height.\n· With “Symmetric” enabled the ratio becomes max/min, so a sudden shrink alarms as well; otherwise only growth alarms.\n· “Minimum alarm box area” filters out the noise of small distant targets; smaller boxes never trigger an alarm.\n· “Alarm sound duration” is how long each red alarm rings; a new alarm restarts the timer instead of layering.\n· The alarm sound uses the system ALARM volume (audible even in silent or DND mode), so make sure that volume is not 0.\n· “Software decode” only affects the built-in RTSP / raw H.264 channel (ExoPlayer manages its own decoder).\n· Transport and decode switches take effect on the next connection.</string>
